WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.557
We have three main choices for reusable query logic.

00:00:03.557 --> 00:00:08.802
A common table expression exists only while one S Q L statement is running.

00:00:08.802 --> 00:00:13.627
It is useful for organizing temporary stages inside that statement.

00:00:13.627 --> 00:00:21.267
A standard view is saved in the database, but it stores the query definition rather than a separate copy of the result.

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:27.277
A materialized view is also saved in the database, but it stores the result itself.

00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:35.097
The choice depends on three questions: how often the logic will be reused, how current the result must be,

00:00:35.097 --> 00:00:37.765
and how expensive the underlying query is.
